WEBVTT

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:04.580
Taiki Aiba
Rui Tomita

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:06.250
Taiki Aiha

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:09.040
then Aiba and Tomita
are the most qualified.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:13.590
If I excuse their bad attitudes as
"unique personalities," these two might just work.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:14.800
Mr. Lucas.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:20.350
The Nemesis Foundation's
technical staff wants to see you.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.430
The foundation's staff?

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:28.440
I assume the chairman sent them
because he heard that you're entering...

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.610
...the Gunpla Battle championship here.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:36.030
I'd rather they just pretend
they're supporting me,

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:39.490
and enjoy sightseeing in Japan.
Can you tell them that?

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.200
Yes, sir.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:47.120
Honestly, Grandpa's so overprotective.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:52.670
"If you want to win at
Gunpla Battle, play it yourself."

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:57.180
You were right, Aila Jyrkiainen.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.590
Something that's this much fun...

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.810
...should be done personally.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:27.120
<i>Our wings couldn't wait for the wind, so we set out</i>

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:32.590
<i>We were bathed in the light of the frozen sun</i>

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:35.340
<i>Oh Oh Oh Oh Oh there are no limits</i>

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:38.090
<i>Oh Oh Oh Oh Oh just let it go</i>

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:43.680
<i>Oh Oh Oh Oh Oh loneliness won't break us</i>

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:48.180
<i>At the end of the dream we'll never give up,</i>

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:50.850
<i>Will there be a future that can never end?</i>

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:56.400
<i>Believe in what only you can do</i>

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.150
<i>If I could seize one thing,</i>

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:01.870
<i>I'd choose it without hesitation</i>

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:07.120
<i>Follow your instincts, just hold on to our bond</i>

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:13.710
Up to the endless sky, now! Fly away

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:35.060
<i>GUNDAM BUILD FIGHTERS TRY</i>

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.440
Sekai, have you finished
filing down those parts?

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:41.820
How's this?

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:45.950
Wow, you brought out
the surfaces properly.

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:47.830
You're unexpectedly skillful.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.620
When I was training with my master,

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:54.170
I prepared the food and
everything else myself.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:55.920
Maybe that's coming in handy.

00:02:57.550 --> 00:02:59.760
How was he spending his life?

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:03.930
When I look at the parts Mr. Sei made,

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:06.890
they're so perfect
that it makes me sigh.

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:10.310
He triumphed in the World Championship...

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:12.980
...with Gunpla he built when he was my age.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:17.440
Putting it in Gundam terms,
Mr. Sei is a monster.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:22.610
Will I ever be able
to build such a piece?

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:26.530
It may take some time,
but I'm sure you will.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:30.790
After all, Gunpla will be with us
for many years to come.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:34.790
You're right.

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:38.590
So, will I be able to build a Gunpla
like the Try Burning someday?

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:39.800
No, never.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:41.170
What?!

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:44.470
Hot-Blooded Gunpla Battle!

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:46.470
Hot-Blooded Gunpla Battle!
Hot-Blooded Gunpla Battle!

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:49.560
<i>Today is the tenth day...</i>

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:52.180
<i>...of the Gunpla Battle Japanese
Under-19 Championship.</i>

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:54.060
<i>The quarterfinals are over,</i>

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:56.020
<i>and the best four have been decided.</i>

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:58.650
<i>Now for the semifinals' highlights.</i>

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:02.490
<i>Mr. Rainer Cziommer, Gunpla Battle
analyst, will tell us everything!</i>

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:05.490
<i>Mr. Cziommer, thank you for coming.</i>

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:08.120
Aren't you going to watch it?

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:10.540
Your favorite Mirai is on.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:12.500
I'm recording it.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:14.330
Of course you are.

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:16.370
The semifinals...

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:20.670
I can't believe our team
is in the national best four.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:24.800
You told me you wanted to play
Gunpla Battle as long as possible.

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.840
That's true, but...

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:28.340
Please wait and see.

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:31.260
I'll make this team...

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:34.270
...the best in Japan, for sure.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:51.200
You look so relaxed.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:58.080
The semifinals start tomorrow
after the brackets are drawn.

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:00.290
This is a celebration.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:02.380
Of your coming championship?

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:06.010
Of the appearance of formidable rivals.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:10.300
When you were Tatsuya Yuuki,
weren't you searching for them?

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:16.230
People with whom you could compete.
People who could help improve each other.

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:18.270
Yeah.

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:22.570
My team members want that, too.

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:28.070
A strong adversary.

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:33.370
An opponent who can
blow away their boredom.

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:39.000
One who's as capable as they are.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:45.880
I hope they'll keep
searching for a challenge.

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:50.050
I hope they won't be satisfied with
being Japan's student champions.

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:52.220
I want them to enter
the Open Tournament...

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.100
...and fly up to the world stage.

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:58.600
The organizer, Yajima Trading,
holds the same hopes.

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:02.810
That's why the National Tournament
is set to damage level A,

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:05.190
as per the international rules.

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:11.410
To boys and girls who want
to fly into the future.

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:14.160
To the future of Gunpla.

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:19.120
Episode 21
Blue Wings

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:24.920
<i>We will now draw lots
to decide the brackets...</i>

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:27.840
<i>...for the Gunpla Battle Japanese
Championship semifinals.</i>

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:35.640
Let the drawing begin!

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:37.640
Ready...

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:39.310
Go!

00:06:40.390 --> 00:06:40.980
Granada Academy

00:06:43.810 --> 00:06:44.060
Gunpla Academy Granada Academy

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:44.650
Gunpla Academy Granada Academy
Tendaiji Academy Seiho Academy

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:46.230
Gunpla Academy Granada Academy

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:46.650
<i>Match One of the semifinals is,</i>

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:49.650
<i>Gunpla Academy,
representing Shizuoka,</i>

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:51.650
<i>team Celestial Sphere versus...</i>

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:54.780
<i>...Granada Academy,
representing Tokushima,</i>

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:56.410
<i>team Von Braun.</i>

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:58.330
<i>Match two is,</i>

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:01.250
<i>Seiho Academy Middle School,
representing West Tokyo,</i>

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:02.920
<i>team Try Fighters versus...</i>

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:05.920
<i>...Tendaiji Academy,
representing Osaka,</i>

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:08.170
<i>team Build Busters.</i>

00:07:11.510 --> 00:07:13.340
Our opponent is...

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:15.600
...Tendaiji Academy?

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:17.600
What a pity.

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:21.930
I expected to fight you
in the semifinals.

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:29.820
As I thought, you're
taking part in the tournament.

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:33.360
I'll postpone the fun
until the final round.

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:34.610
That won't happen.

00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:37.620
In the final round,
Sekai's team will be fighting...

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:40.080
...against us, the Gunpla Academy.

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:43.210
Our apologies to the European champion,

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:45.290
but we can't let you win this one.

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:47.210
I'm afraid that...

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:50.300
...your wishes will vanish
into the ether.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:55.220
The Try Fighters are destined
to lose to us in the semifinals.

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:56.510
I can't allow that.

00:07:57.550 --> 00:07:58.890
We're going to win.

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:01.720
We also have a reason
why we can't lose.

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:06.900
That's enough.

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:09.730
What are you all going on about?

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:12.320
Things are simple.

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:15.240
Strong ones win, weak ones lose.

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:17.820
That's all there is to it.

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:19.830
You're right.

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:21.540
It's nice and simple.

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:24.710
I have some preparation to do.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:27.630
Best of luck to you all.

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:33.260
Let's go to our waiting room, too.

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:36.550
We'll keep tuning our Gunpla
right up until match two.

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:37.430
Sure.

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:38.390
Okay!

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:44.930
The battle of Gunpla Academy
and Granada Academy.

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:47.600
Which do you think
will win, Toshi?

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:49.480
The Gunpla Academy.

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:53.860
Granada's addition of a helper
won't shake up their strength.

00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:55.030
Gabai Institute

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:55.780
Gabai Institute

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:57.820
Most people expect
the Gunpla Academy to win.

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:01.780
But we actually fought him,
so we know better.

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:05.580
Lucas Nemesis' strength
is unbelievable.

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:10.630
There's a good possibility
of a stunning upset.

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:15.300
<i>We now begin match one.</i>

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:18.680
<i>Gunpla Academy,
representing Shizuoka,</i>

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:20.680
<i>team Celestial Sphere versus...</i>

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:23.720
<i>...Granada Academy,
representing Tokushima,</i>

00:09:23.720 --> 00:09:26.640
<i>team Von Braun.</i>

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:30.020
Gunpla Academy Granada Academy

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:32.440
Aiba, Tomita,

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:35.480
please do as I just told you.

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:38.490
I can't believe you picked
us two benchwarmers.

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:40.740
You must be really
confident, Mr. Champion.

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:43.490
That's because I decided...

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:46.660
...that you would be the most
capable of carrying out my tactics.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.290
The coach gave his approval.

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:51.080
So let's do our best out there.

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:52.710
I'll do whatever it takes.

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:56.260
I'd never pass up a chance
to beat the Gunpla Academy.

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:58.170
That's fine by me.

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:02.760
A battle against the European champion.

00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:08.680
This will be a good test of our
readiness for the Open Tournament.

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:13.150
Let's show the world the ability
of the Gunpla Academy.

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:14.270
Okay, Brother.

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:16.190
I can't wait another instant.

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:19.700
This fight needs no commentary.

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:22.070
Just watch carefully.

00:10:22.070 --> 00:10:23.200
Yes.

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:27.330
<i>Gunpla Battle, combat mode, startup.</i>

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:30.120
<i>Model damage level, set to A.</i>

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:32.750
Please set your GP Base.

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:40.050
<i>Beginning Plavsky particle dispersal.</i>

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:46.510
<i>Field 8, Sky.</i>

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:48.980
Please set your Gunpla.

00:10:56.770 --> 00:10:58.280
<i>Battle start.</i>

00:10:58.570 --> 00:11:01.240
Wilfrid Kijima, Transient Gundam.

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:04.200
Saga Adou, Gundam The End.

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:06.530
Shia Kijima, G-Portent.

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:09.910
Team Celestial Sphere, fly away!

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:16.420
Let's do it as planned.

00:11:17.210 --> 00:11:20.170
Team Von Braun, Lucas Nemesis.

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:23.090
Crossbone X1 Full Cloth.

00:11:24.340 --> 00:11:25.260
Here I go!

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:42.820
The Full Cloth is approaching first?

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:46.530
Does he intend to fight us alone?

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:51.540
What a sweet-looking move.

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:53.290
Go, fangs!

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:15.560
All with one shot?!

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:18.480
<i>More!</i>

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:24.780
How about this?!

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:41.590
Adou!

00:12:41.750 --> 00:12:42.550
Mr. Adou!

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:52.560
You're good. Very nice!

00:12:54.430 --> 00:12:55.640
It transformed?

00:12:56.140 --> 00:12:58.900
Now, I'll go all out!

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:04.240
Very nice!

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:06.860
I've been waiting for
an opponent like you!

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:14.200
Not bad.

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:18.330
Kijima!

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:24.170
The Full Cloth was
made for high gravity.

00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:27.090
<i>Considering its high thrust...</i>

00:13:28.630 --> 00:13:29.800
<i>There!</i>

00:13:49.780 --> 00:13:51.320
That was skillful.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:55.410
Quick hands, too.

00:13:58.870 --> 00:14:00.290
I'll join Aiba's machine.

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:05.250
<i>The enemy made a hole.</i>

00:14:05.250 --> 00:14:06.590
<i>Can I use it?</i>

00:14:07.470 --> 00:14:08.800
<i>Did you get him?</i>

00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:10.470
<i>No, there's no reaction.</i>

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:14.600
The firepower and mobility
of the Full Cloth are outstanding.

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:17.810
Where is that machine storing
such a huge amount of particles?

00:14:21.270 --> 00:14:22.810
Only one machine is coming out.

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:24.440
Shia, I'll leave it to you.

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:25.480
What will you do, Brother?

00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:28.240
<i>I'm going to back up Adou.
It's too much for him alone.</i>

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:29.320
<i>Roger that.</i>

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:36.200
You can't hit me.

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:45.000
Another one from behind?

00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:49.630
The Full Cloth's core fighter?!

00:14:50.170 --> 00:14:51.550
A particle transformation field?

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:55.140
That function should have
been omitted from the HG.

00:14:55.350 --> 00:14:57.180
What craftsmanship!

00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:07.190
Don't chase her too far!

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:09.780
<i>Stay at your assigned point!</i>

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:10.780
Roger that.

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:14.030
<i>Big Brother.</i>

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:15.280
What's wrong, Shia?

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:16.700
The Full Cloth got me.

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:17.910
<i>What? !</i>

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:19.660
<i>He went around to your side?</i>

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:22.370
He used the hole you made.

00:15:24.630 --> 00:15:25.420
What?

00:15:25.830 --> 00:15:27.420
He's already back?!

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:32.550
Why does it have such
high particle emission?

00:15:33.510 --> 00:15:34.590
Could it be...?

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:35.550
Pursue him!

00:15:35.800 --> 00:15:36.720
<i>Roger.</i>

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:45.900
If you think you've defeated me,
you're greatly mistaken.

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:06.250
<i>We're ready!</i>

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:07.590
I'm going to dock.

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:18.260
He chased me,
even knowing his disadvantage?

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:20.760
Did he guess our strategy?

00:16:21.060 --> 00:16:21.770
Aiba!

00:16:21.970 --> 00:16:23.560
Go to the next supply point.

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:25.560
You're such a slave driver.

00:16:30.770 --> 00:16:31.820
<i>Pincer attack.</i>

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:32.780
<i>Okay!</i>

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:48.790
Gotcha!

00:16:56.130 --> 00:16:56.880
What?!

00:16:59.890 --> 00:17:01.350
He repelled our attack?!

00:17:01.470 --> 00:17:02.470
Not yet!

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:06.850
Dead End...

00:17:08.900 --> 00:17:09.860
l-field!

00:17:09.980 --> 00:17:11.650
<i>-..Finger!!</i>

00:17:15.490 --> 00:17:16.360
<i>With this...</i>

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:26.370
This is as far as you get.

00:17:34.510 --> 00:17:36.170
The output's not falling.

00:17:36.670 --> 00:17:38.260
There must be some trick.

00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:49.480
The Full Cloth's particle count
isn't decreasing...

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:52.610
...and the other machines
aren't coming out to fight.

00:17:53.650 --> 00:17:54.690
I see...!

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:56.360
I get it now!

00:17:58.570 --> 00:18:01.660
<i>Compressed particle
transmission rate is 26 percent.</i>

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:03.780
I'm grateful that you're
acting as my support.

00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:06.120
<i>Just be sure to show us results!</i>

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:12.290
They're resupplying his particles.

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:14.460
This is sooner than I expected...

00:18:15.050 --> 00:18:15.960
Tomita!

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:17.380
Go to Aiba!

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:18.720
<i>I've got this!</i>

00:18:21.050 --> 00:18:22.390
You think you're smart, huh?

00:18:25.810 --> 00:18:27.220
I told you.

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:29.390
<i>I won't let you go!</i>

00:18:31.810 --> 00:18:32.860
<i>The Full Cloth!</i>

00:18:33.150 --> 00:18:34.440
How dare you...!

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:51.250
Sorry, Tomita.

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:52.460
<i>Nemesis!</i>

00:18:54.290 --> 00:18:55.250
<i>Over here.</i>

00:19:08.430 --> 00:19:09.850
That machine is...!

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:13.770
Don't underestimate my G-Portent.

00:19:15.810 --> 00:19:18.320
But you were fatally damaged.

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:23.360
Three-on-one.

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:28.120
But I can't give up just yet!

00:19:29.240 --> 00:19:31.870
Big Brother, there's
only two minutes left.

00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:34.460
We'll win if we just stay alive.

00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:36.000
<i>Don't be stupid, Shia!</i>

00:19:36.590 --> 00:19:37.960
Adou is right.

00:19:38.630 --> 00:19:41.800
I don't want such an incomplete victory.

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:43.800
<i>Go, Kijima.</i>

00:19:44.680 --> 00:19:46.300
<i>I'll let you finish it.</i>

00:19:53.480 --> 00:19:54.520
I appreciate it.

00:19:54.900 --> 00:19:56.480
Let's go, Transient!

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:00.980
A one-on-one duel?

00:20:02.690 --> 00:20:04.950
He has that much confidence, huh?

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:06.160
Or maybe,

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:09.490
just like me,

00:20:09.950 --> 00:20:11.870
he's a serious Gunpla freak!

00:20:12.330 --> 00:20:13.750
If I might be so bold...

00:20:13.830 --> 00:20:15.250
It's the latter!

00:20:26.550 --> 00:20:27.800
<i>Full Mode!</i>

00:20:31.520 --> 00:20:35.310
Transient... Burst!

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:53.700
That glow...

00:20:56.540 --> 00:21:01.000
These are our wings
to fly to the future!

00:21:17.140 --> 00:21:20.190
The shining light
that leads to the future...

00:21:27.110 --> 00:21:28.660
Why is everyone cheering?

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:39.790
<i>There's a tomorrow I want to touch</i>

00:21:39.790 --> 00:21:43.170
<i>I want to prove it for myself</i>

00:21:43.170 --> 00:21:47.970
<i>Love, hate, which is it?</i>

00:21:48.760 --> 00:21:51.800
<i>Perhaps the challenge is in the journey</i>

00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:54.930
<i>Wandering the unknown path...</i>

00:21:54.930 --> 00:22:01.650
<i>...toward abundant happiness</i>

00:22:03.440 --> 00:22:06.400
<i>I was afraid to run</i>

00:22:06.400 --> 00:22:09.780
<i>But now that I've started, I can't stop</i>

00:22:09.780 --> 00:22:12.620
<i>I must've been waiting for the go sign</i>

00:22:12.620 --> 00:22:16.450
<i>With this passion in my impatient heart,</i>

00:22:16.450 --> 00:22:21.120
<i>I want to search for something</i>

00:22:21.120 --> 00:22:25.840
<i>Let's meet over and over again (with you)</i>

00:22:25.840 --> 00:22:28.130
<i>On this journey, can you show me...</i>

00:22:28.130 --> 00:22:33.180
<i>...a different truth? (let me see)</i>

00:22:33.180 --> 00:22:40.140
<i>The power to find new things (with me)</i>

00:22:40.140 --> 00:22:43.690
<i>Never forget it</i>

00:22:43.690 --> 00:22:45.980
<i>Bring the real you to meet the real me</i>

00:22:45.980 --> 00:22:46.530
<i>(Today)
Bring the real you to meet the real me</i>

00:22:46.530 --> 00:22:48.150
<i>(Today)
As we travel, you smile at me</i>

00:22:48.150 --> 00:22:49.030
<i>(I'll be there...)
As we travel, you smile at me</i>

00:22:49.030 --> 00:22:52.030
<i>(I'll be there...)
I love it, I love it, this journey without a compass</i>

00:22:52.030 --> 00:22:54.410
<i>(Alive!)
I love it, I love it, this journey without a compass</i>

00:22:54.410 --> 00:22:55.370
<i>(Alive!)</i>

00:22:55.410 --> 00:23:01.330
Team Try Fighters!

00:23:05.250 --> 00:23:07.340
Who... Who won?

00:23:08.880 --> 00:23:10.170
That's...

00:23:23.650 --> 00:23:26.270
Wilfrid Kijima's Gunpla...

00:23:27.110 --> 00:23:28.940
That guy beat him?

00:23:30.400 --> 00:23:32.110
Lucas Nemesis won?!

00:23:42.580 --> 00:23:43.920
Congratulations.

00:23:44.880 --> 00:23:46.630
You're the winner.

00:23:56.220 --> 00:23:58.140
<i>Battle ended.</i>

00:24:00.560 --> 00:24:02.180
To be yourself.

00:24:02.180 --> 00:24:03.810
To keep loving Gunpla.

00:24:03.810 --> 00:24:05.270
Next episode, "Follow Your Heart".

00:24:05.270 --> 00:24:05.850
Follow Your Heart
Next episode, "Follow Your Heart".

00:24:05.850 --> 00:24:10.070
Follow Your Heart
How quickly you can forget such simple things...
